Binding to a non-local address (e.g. `--host 0.0.0.0` inside Docker)
requires the `MCP_ALLOWED_HOSTS` environment variable — the SDK only arms its
DNS-rebinding protection for localhost binds, so `mcp_server.py` refuses to
start without an explicit host allowlist. Health checks live at `GET /health`
(unauthenticated, for the orchestrator; custom routes bypass the allowlist by
design); `mcp-server-{{ repo_name }} --help` lists the `--host` / `--port`
options. See `.env.example` for the variables.

